            0.852
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You will see that white silver chloride turns grey in sunlight. This is due to the decomposition of silver chloride into silver and chlorine by light.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.73,
            0.8,
            0.926,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Silver chloride turns grey in sunlight to form silver metal"
            }
          ]
        },
